What are http verbs and http methods ?
===================================
HTTP verbs (also called HTTP methods) define the action a client wants to perform on a resource in an API.
They describe what operation should be done on the server.
🔹 Common HTTP Methods
GET – Retrieve data from the server
POST – Create new data
PUT – Update an existing resource (full update)
PATCH – Update part of a resource
DELETE – Remove a resource

